    <div class="col-12 value content common-desc-text pb-3 pt-lg-0" id="collapsible-details-1">
        <p>A whole bird is the most versatile dinner in the freezer. This chicken comes cleaned and trimmed with the giblets and neck already removed, so it goes straight from thawed to seasoned to roasting pan.</p>
<p>Roast it whole for a Sunday dinner, spatchcock it for the grill, or break it down into eight pieces for frying and braising. Save the carcass afterwards for a rich homemade stock.</p>
<p>For the crispiest skin, pat the bird dry, season it generously and let it sit uncovered in the refrigerator for a few hours before roasting. Rest the chicken for 15 minutes after it comes out of the oven so the juices settle before carving.</p>
<h3>Serving Ideas</h3>
<ul>
<li>Classic herb-and-lemon roast chicken with root vegetables</li>
<li>Spatchcocked and grilled with a garlic-paprika rub</li>
<li>Slow-cooker whole chicken for shredding into tacos and soups</li>
</ul>
